                <pb facs="0260" n="246" sameAs="frus:frus1947v05/pg246"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.00/7–1947: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Mission for Aid
                        to Greece </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-07-19T19:00:00-04:00">July 19, 1947—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1089. Gama No. 10. For Griswold from McGhee. House Appropriations Subcommittee
                    approved yesterday full $400,000,000 for Assistance to Greece and Turkey under
                    Public Law 75, limiting administrative expenses of Mission to $3,500,000 and
                    administrative expenses in District of Columbia to $300,000 and expressing
                    displeasure at program for training of Greeks in United States and elaborate
                    Mission staff to encourage the promotion of industrial labor relations in
                    Greece. Department appealed administrative cuts before Senate Appropriations
                    Subcommittee this afternoon. Sending by mail House Subcommittee testimony and
                    report and will advise of final Senate Subcommittee and Congressional action and
                    analysis of effect on Mission. [McGhee]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
